<Layout title="Beyond code" description="Debate, theatre, teaching and community: the experiences that shape how Tanzil Ahmed builds.">
  <div class="container page-body"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The other parts of the picture</p><h1>A life beyond<br/>the <span class="serif-word">editor.</span></h1><p>The things I do away from a screen shape the things I bring back to it. A few of those threads.</p></header>
    <div class="life-stories"><section class="life-story" id="debate"><span class="life-number">01 /</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Debate & leadership</p><h2>Learning to ask<br/><span class="serif-word">better questions.</span></h2><p>Debating taught me to build an argument, listen to another one, and change my mind when the evidence calls for it. Founding and leading the debating club at Faizur Rahman Ideal Institute also meant bringing people together and making events happen.</p><p>It became a place where my interests met: tournament workflows inspired Tanzilbot and the deployment work around Tabbycat.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/?category=Earlier+work">Explore the earlier tools<Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div><div class="life-art debate-art" aria-hidden="true"><span>Listen.</span><span>Question.</span><span>Understand.</span><span class="art-plus">↗</span></div></section>
    <section class="life-story" id="theatre"><span class="life-number">02 /</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Theatre & mime</p><h2>A different way<br/>to <span class="serif-word">see.</span></h2><p>Through Duronto Cultural Academy and Gollachut Natyadol, theatre and mime became another way to explore a story. Performance asks you to pay attention to timing, expression and what an audience understands without an explanation.</p><p>I carry that attention into interfaces, too: what a person notices, what feels natural, and what a small detail can communicate.</p></div><div class="life-art theatre-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="theatre-line"></span><span>Another<br/>perspective.</span><span class="art-plus">✳</span></div></section>
    <section class="life-story" id="teaching"><span class="life-number">03 /</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Teaching & community</p><h2>Leave a little<br/><span class="serif-word">light on.</span></h2><p>Learning something becomes more valuable when you can help someone else begin. Through BECEF Network, Bangla tutorials and community activities, I’ve worked on making technology a little more approachable.</p><p>Volunteering with Phulkuri Ashar and experiences in Bangladesh Scouts are also part of that story: useful work happens when people show up for each other.</p><a class="text-link" href="/open-source/">Resources I’ve contributed<Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></div><div class="life-art teaching-art" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="sprout" size={100}/><span>Learn.<br/>Share.<br/>Repeat.</span></div></section></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
